  "result": "Perfect! All 183 tests pass. The customer statements feature is now complete.\n\n**Summary of implementation:**\n\n**src/statements.js** \u2014 New module with `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function that:\n- Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })` on success\n- Normalizes customer ID using `normalizeId()`\n- Validates customer exists (returns CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND if not)\n- Filters invoices by:\n  - Customer ID match\n  - Status is 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes draft and paid)\n  - issueDate is on or before asOf date\n- Maps each invoice to: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n  - `due` calculated via `balanceDue()` to account for payments and vouchers\n- Sorts results by issueDate\n- Calculates `totalDue` as sum of all individual dues\n\n**test/statements.test.js** \u2014 16 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Empty statements and filtering logic\n- Error handling (CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND)\n- ID normalization\n- Status filtering (issued/partially_paid included, paid/draft excluded)\n- Date filtering (only on or before asOf)\n- Sorting and calculation accuracy\n- Multi-customer isolation\n- Partial payments and voucher impact on due amounts",
